If you're going to exploit the non-randomness of the random number
generator, why not go whole hog?

Figure out where you are in the cycle by observing the behavior of
the game and then tailor your actions to always produce the desired
results -- delaying an attack if need be to get the right roll.

If you don't do this, the cyclic nature of the RNG doesn't neccessarily
save you.  You need it to cycle in synchronization with the game's
state.  If, on cycle 1, RNG # 1 is a fire giant spawn roll
and on cycle 2, RNG #1 is a fire giant attack roll, the cycle isn't
buying you anything.

